      "category": "numerical",
      "difficulty": 1,
      "marks": 3,
      "stem": "Supplementary (Zhao, Ch. 6). Apply the Robbins–Monro iteration $w_{k+1} = w_k - a_k\\tilde g(w_k)$ to $g(w) = w - 10$ with no noise, $w_1 = 20$ and $a_k = 0.5$. Find $w_2$, $w_3$ and $w_4$.",
      "parts": [
        { "label": "w_2", "answer": 15, "tolerance": 0.001 },
        { "label": "w_3", "answer": 12.5, "tolerance": 0.001 },
        { "label": "w_4", "answer": 11.25, "tolerance": 0.001 }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "$w_2 = 20 - 0.5(20 - 10) = 15$.",
        "$w_3 = 15 - 0.5(15 - 10) = 12.5$.",
        "$w_4 = 12.5 - 0.5(12.5 - 10) = 11.25$."
      ],
      "explanation": "Each step halves the distance to the root $w^* = 10$.",
      "sources": [{ "kind": "lecture", "lecture": "L6", "slides": [21, 21] }],
